## Ontology Generate — semantic relation deduplication (no paraphrased or inverse duplicates)

Context: Ontology > Generate (Stage 3 relations) could create the same fact twice, e.g. `Contract --settledBy--> Payment` plus `Contract --isSettledBy--> Payment`, or `Payment --settles--> Contract` next to an inverse restatement. The previous pair-level inverse collapse kept every label on the winning direction (so paraphrases survived), dropped distinct facts on the reverse direction, and ignored relations already present in the ontology. Policy agreed with the user: remove only semantic duplicates and inverses; keep distinct business relations on the same entity pair. Design: `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-30-generate-relation-semantic-dedup-design.md`.

Changes:
1. `src/agents/agent_owl_generator/RelationDeduplicator.py` (new) — `RelationDeduplicator` computes a semantic key (unordered entity pair + verb core with copulas, trailing `by`/`of` and inflections stripped; cores under 4 chars fall back to an exact directed key so ambiguous stems are kept) and `dedupe(relations, existing=...)` keeps one active-voice relation per key and drops restatements of existing relations. Hosts the former `_relation_voice_score` as `voice_score`.
2. `src/agents/agent_owl_generator/schemas.py` — `drop_inverse_relations` is now a delegator to `RelationDeduplicator.dedupe`; `parse_relations_payload(text, existing=())` dedupes against existing relations too.
3. `src/agents/agent_owl_generator/prompts.py` — relations system prompt: one fact = one relation, no inverse or paraphrase in either direction, active voice, distinct facts on the same pair allowed, never restate an existing property. `build_relations_user_prompt(draft, existing_relations=())` adds an "EXISTING OBJECT PROPERTIES" block when non-empty.
4. `src/agents/agent_owl_generator/staged.py` — `infer_relations` reads `options["existing_relations"]`, shows them in the prompt and filters restatements at parse time.
5. `src/back/objects/ontology/GenerateWorkflow.py` — `run_completion` passes existing anchor-to-anchor object properties to the relations substage; `merge_draft_into_ontology` replaces the directed-pair inverse drop with semantic keys over existing properties and relations accepted earlier in the same merge (distinct reverse predicates are now kept).
6. Eval: `tests/eval/staged_contract.py` (new parser-level check `_c_relation_dedup` for kinds `collapses_passive_paraphrase`, `collapses_inverse_paraphrase`, `keeps_distinct_predicates_same_pair`, `keeps_existing_ontology_relation`); `tests/eval/run_agent_owl_generator.py` (floor 18 → 28, the 4 kinds required); 10 new rows `staged-relation-dedup-001..010` in `tests/eval/datasets/agent_owl_generator/baseline.jsonl` and the byte-identical mirror `.planning/agents/agent_owl_generator/eval/dataset.jsonl`.
7. `.planning/agents/agent_owl_generator/SPEC.md` — new §6 failure-mode row and §10 sign-off entry.
8. Tests: `tests/units/agents/test_relation_deduplicator.py` (new, 13), `tests/units/agents/test_owl_generator_schemas.py` (+3), `tests/units/agents/test_owl_generator_staged.py` (+4), `tests/units/ontology/test_generate_workflow.py` (+4: existing relations wired to the relations runner, semantic merge).
9. `docs/sphinx/api/agents.rst` — documents the new module; spec typo fixed.

